  "issue": {
    "body": "## Description  \nOn the [Starlette Sponsorship Page](https://www.starlette.io/sponsorship/), the text in the **Sponsorship tier cards** (Bronze, Silver, Gold) is difficult to read due to **low contrast** between the text and background. This impacts accessibility and readability, especially for the Silver and Gold tiers where text appears very faint.  \n\n## Screenshot  \n\n<img width=\"1372\" height=\"1260\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3724dd4b-24ab-4549-856e-0044a7caba4e\" />\n\n## Problems Identified  \n- \u274c Text color is too light, reducing readability.  \n- \u274c Some benefits are nearly invisible without straining.  \n- \u274c Accessibility guidelines (WCAG contrast ratio) may not be met.  \n\n## Suggested Fixes  \n- Use **higher contrast text colors** (e.g., darker shades).  \n- Ensure **minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1** for normal text, 3:1 for large text (WCAG 2.1 AA compliance).  \n- Consider **hover states or tooltips** to make benefits clearer.  \n- Add an **accessible mode toggle** (dark/light contrast safe mode).  \n\n## Impact  \nImproving readability will:  \n- \u2705 Enhance user experience.  \n- \u2705 Ensure accessibility compliance.  \n- \u2705 Increase likelihood of potential sponsors engaging with the tiers.  \n",
    "closed_at": "2025-10-19T09:58:41Z",
